<% content_for :title, 'Library' %>

<%= render 'help/page', title: 'Library' do %>
  <div class='space-y-8'>

    <p class='text-fg-muted'>
      Rulebooks are uploaded once into a global catalog shared across every campaign. The
      Library lists every rulebook in that catalog and lets this campaign's referee choose
      which of those books this campaign actually uses. A book must be enabled here before it
      appears in this campaign's rulebook search.
    </p>

    <div>
      <dl class='space-y-6'>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Title / Category / Edition</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Metadata describing the rulebook, set by the administrator who imported it.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Enabled</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Whether this campaign uses the book. When on, the referee can find it in rulebook
            search. Turning it off also clears
            <span class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Player Searchable</span> for that book.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Player Searchable</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Of the enabled books, which are also visible to players — anonymous, not-logged-in
            visitors. This app has no separate player-account system; "not logged in" is the
            player role. A book can't be player-searchable without also being enabled;
            switching this on enables the book automatically if it wasn't already.
          </dd>
        </div>

      </dl>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p class='text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-highlight mb-4'>Not Seeing a Book?</p>
      <p class='text-fg'>
        Only rulebooks an administrator has marked <span class='font-mono text-fg-bright'>Searchable</span>
        and finished importing appear here. If a book you expect is missing, ask an
        administrator to check its status in the rulebook catalog.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class='pt-2 text-right uppercase font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.22em] text-fg-muted'>
      REFERENCE 0804LB
    </div>

  </div>
<% end %>
